findings.body:
The PR fixes the NPE in getSubGroupsCount() by guarding the result of modelSupplier.get() with a null check, but the same race that produces null in getSubGroupsCount() still applies to the three getSubGroupsStream overloads at lines 254-269:

  return modelSupplier.get().getSubGroupsStream(search, firstResult, maxResults);
  return modelSupplier.get().getSubGroupsStream(firstResult, maxResults);
  return modelSupplier.get().getSubGroupsStream(search, exact, firstResult, maxResults);

If a GroupAdapter exists in the cache for a group that has just been deleted, cacheSession.getGroupDelegate().getGroupById(...) returns null, so modelSupplier.get() returns null and the chained .getSubGroupsStream(...) throws NullPointerException immediately. This is the exact same concurrency scenario the PR claims to address, and the new test createMultiDeleteMultiReadMulti can still hit it through any code path that lists subgroups of a deleted group's cached adapter. The fix must be applied consistently (either guard every modelSupplier.get() result, or push the null-handling down into the LazyLoader so the adapter cannot return null source data).
